From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TofuJoe <darryl.hon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:43:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] drm/xe/guc: Skip the 1 us teardown preemption for idle
 exec queues

disable_scheduling_deregister() always sends a 1 us preemption-timeout
policy for the context before the SCHED_CONTEXT_MODE_SET(DISABLE) +
DEREGISTER pair, so a context that is still executing is taken off the
hardware without waiting for its normal preemption timeout.

On ADL-P (GuC 70.49.4) that request makes the GuC reset an engine even
when the context has nothing to preempt: rcs queues that live 2-5 ms and
never ran work (Nautilus, Wine, Xwayland startup) produce "Engine reset
... state=0x3" followed by a "Timedout job" for seqno
XE_FENCE_INITIAL_SEQNO, often attributed to a different, idle queue of the
same process. Harmless but noisy.

(A separate vcs failure, "GuC engine reset request failed" followed by a
full GT reset under heavy VA decoder churn, also reproduces with this
patch applied and with a stock module; this patch does not address it.)

Only send the 1 us policy when the queue may still be executing: when not
every emitted job has written its completion seqno
(xe_exec_queue_is_idle()), or the queue is reset, banned or wedged, or it
is part of a multi-queue group. "Killed" cannot be used as the criterion,
because every user close kills the queue.

The check is race-free: it runs from the CLEANUP message, after the last
queue reference is gone. Every job holds a queue reference, so no job can
be armed or submitted any more and the seqno only moves forward; an idle
answer cannot become stale. A stale read of the seqno map only makes the
queue look busy, which keeps the old behaviour. A job armed but never run
also keeps the old behaviour. The seqno is written by the last flush's
post-sync, after which the ring holds only MI_USER_INTERRUPT, so the
queue's normal preemption timeout (640 ms here) never comes into play for
an idle context and teardown latency does not change in practice.

Disable at runtime with xe.skip_idle_teardown_preempt=0.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.c     |  5 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.h     |  1 +
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c
index b9e9cf5..6466d5b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_guc_submit.c
@@ -1268,13 +1268,46 @@ static void handle_deregister_done(struct xe_guc *guc, struct xe_exec_queue *q);
 		GUC_CONTEXT_##enable_disable,				\
 	}
 
+/*
+ * The 1 us preemption timeout before the teardown disable exists to get a
+ * context that is still executing off the hardware without waiting for its
+ * normal preemption timeout. A queue whose every emitted job has already
+ * written its completion seqno has nothing left to preempt, and on ADL-P the
+ * GuC sometimes answers the 1 us request with an engine reset that fails on a
+ * video engine (escalating to a full GT reset) or that is attributed to an
+ * unrelated idle queue on rcs. Skip it for such queues and let the queue's
+ * normal policy apply to the disable.
+ *
+ * This runs from the CLEANUP message, i.e. after the last reference to the
+ * queue was dropped. Every job holds a queue reference, so no job can be
+ * created or armed any more and the seqno can only move forward: an idle
+ * answer cannot become stale. A stale read of the seqno map only makes the
+ * queue look busy, which keeps the old behaviour.
+ */
+static bool teardown_needs_min_preemption(struct xe_exec_queue *q)
+{
+	if (!xe_modparam.skip_idle_teardown_preempt)
+		return true;
+
+	/* Reset, banned or wedged: the hardware state is not trustworthy */
+	if (exec_queue_reset(q) || exec_queue_banned(q) || exec_queue_wedged(q))
+		return true;
+
+	/* The policy of a group primary covers the whole group */
+	if (xe_exec_queue_is_multi_queue(q))
+		return true;
+
+	return !xe_exec_queue_is_idle(q);
+}
+
 static void disable_scheduling_deregister(struct xe_guc *guc,
 					  struct xe_exec_queue *q)
 {
 	MAKE_SCHED_CONTEXT_ACTION(q, DISABLE);
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!xe_exec_queue_is_multi_queue_secondary(q))
+	if (!xe_exec_queue_is_multi_queue_secondary(q) &&
+	    teardown_needs_min_preemption(q))
 		set_min_preemption_timeout(guc, q);
 
 	smp_rmb();
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.c
index 2bf45f2..b16687d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ struct xe_modparam xe_modparam = {
 	.svm_notifier_size =	XE_DEFAULT_SVM_NOTIFIER_SIZE,
 	.flip_boost =		true,
 	.tlb_inval_coalesce =	true,
+	.skip_idle_teardown_preempt = true,
 	.shrink_active_ms =	1000,
 	.prefault_pages =	512,
 	/* the rest are 0 by default */
@@ -58,6 +59,10 @@ module_param_named(tlb_inval_coalesce, xe_modparam.tlb_inval_coalesce, bool, 060
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(tlb_inval_coalesce, "On GPUs without range TLB invalidation, merge full PPGTT "
 		 "TLB invalidations requested while one is still in flight [default=true]");
 
+module_param_named(skip_idle_teardown_preempt, xe_modparam.skip_idle_teardown_preempt, bool, 0600);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(skip_idle_teardown_preempt, "When destroying an exec queue whose jobs have all completed, "
+		 "don't ask the GuC to preempt it within 1 us first [default=true]");
+
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DRM_XE_DISPLAY)
 module_param_named(probe_display, xe_modparam.probe_display, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(probe_display, "Probe display HW, otherwise it's left untouched "
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.h
index 1dc29fa..b8a2574 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_module.h
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ struct xe_modparam {
 	u32 svm_notifier_size;
 	bool flip_boost;
 	bool tlb_inval_coalesce;
+	bool skip_idle_teardown_preempt;
 	unsigned int shrink_active_ms;
 	unsigned int prefault_pages;
 };
